From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:01:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: spoof Chrome 155 Client Hint brands natively

Pin the branded Chrome identity to 155.0.8059.40, published for macOS
on October 6, 2026 and matching the embedded V8 15.5 release family.
Keep the MacBook Neo/A18 Pro/8GB/256GB hardware persona unchanged.
This patch deliberately does not change the default UA, platform or
architecture hints, CDP identity, or Client Hint transport opt-in rules.

Use Chromium's seed-155 brand order and GREASE values: Google Chrome,
Chromium, Not(A:Brand; major versions 155/155/24 and corresponding full
versions 155.0.8059.40/155.0.8059.40/24.0.0.0. Derive HTTP and JS lists
from the same definition. Separate low-entropy major versions from
fullVersionList and select uaFullVersion independently of GREASE order.

Preserve native accessors and operations. Capture the native Object.freeze
per context before page scripts run to implement the brands FrozenArray
without trusting mutable page globals. Leave JSON and promise arrays
mutable. Honor requested high-entropy hints, use the formFactors spelling,
and remove the empty-object binding shortcut so wrong receivers reject.

Adjust only existing navigator/fetch/XHR expectations; retain fixed Sec-*
header protection checks and unrelated User-Agent expectations. Temporary
ignored diagnostics verify native descriptors/receiver checks, freezing and
intrinsic tampering, exact hint subsets, HTTP parity, worker reuse and
recreated frame/page contexts. Existing 1658 upstream tests pass.

References:
https://chromereleases.googleblog.com/2026/10/stable-channel-update-for-desktop_086471744.html
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_ua_data.idl
https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/
